[54.563, "o", "\r\nApply 14 label change(s) and 2 comment(s):\r\n\r\n  1. #1  labels: bug\r\n  2. #2  labels: bug\r\n  3. #3  labels: enhancement\r\n  4. #4  labels: enhancement\r\n  5. #5  labels: question\r\n  6. #6  labels: bug\r\n  7. #7  labels: enhancement\r\n  8. #8  labels: documentation\r\n  9. #9  labels: question\r\n 10. #10  labels: enhancement\r\n 11. #11  labels: bug, duplicate\r\n 12. #12  labels: enhancement, duplicate\r\n 13. #13  labels: documentation, good first issue\r\n 14. #14  labels: enhancement\r\n 15. #11  comment:\r\n       Thanks for the report! This looks like a duplicate of #1, which describes the same Windows UnicodeEncodeError when listing a habit name containing an emoji. We\u2019ll track the issue there.\r\n 16. #12  comment:\r\n       Thanks for the report! This looks like a duplicate of #4, which requests exporting check-in history as CSV for spreadsheet use. We\u2019ll track the export request there.\r\n"]
